# The remaining shared ledgers use git's built-in union merge driver:
# overlapping additions from two branches are concatenated instead of
# conflicting. This is only safe under the editing protocol in CLAUDE.md
# (self-contained sections, no in-place edits in the same PR as an
# addition). NOTE: GitHub's merge button ignores merge attributes — when a PR
# shows a conflict in one of these files, resolve with a local
# `git merge origin/main`, which applies the driver and auto-resolves.
# (Changelog entries and FEATURES notes now live as one file per PR in
# changelog/, so they can't conflict at all; FEATURES.md is generated.)
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
decision_log.md merge=union
